<% set_page_meta title: "README", description: "About SPEERD and the practice connecting light, costume, code, and metal." %>

<main id="main-content">
  <header class="page-hero about-hero accent--electric">
    <div class="page-hero__copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">About the maker</p>
      <h1>README</h1>
      <p class="page-hero__lede">SPEERD is a workshop practice for objects that sit between engineering, craft, and performance.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="about-hero__code" aria-hidden="true">
      <span>01 / IMAGINE</span>
      <span>02 / PROTOTYPE</span>
      <span>03 / BREAK</span>
      <span>04 / BUILD BETTER</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="about-grid" aria-labelledby="about-practice-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The practice</p>
      <h2 id="about-practice-title">Different materials. Same curiosity.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>I build responsive LED art, overcommitted costumes, and wearable metalwork. The disciplines look unrelated until the workbench fills up: each needs a feel for systems, materials, human movement, and the precise moment when restraint stops being useful.</p>
      <p>This site is a living record of finished pieces and the decisions behind them. The project pages tell the story; the galleries hold the close looks, strange details, and proof that the thing really worked.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="principles" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Workshop notes</p>
    <h2 id="principles-title">A few things I believe.</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><span>01</span> The engineering should serve the experience.</li>
      <li><span>02</span> A prop is not finished until a person can live in it.</li>
      <li><span>03</span> Serviceability is a design feature.</li>
      <li><span>04</span> There is always room for one more light.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <%= render "shared/contact_cta" %>
</main>
